// A Read is permitted if there was formerly a Login. The policy predicate
// does NOT mention `callerPrincipal` — but the event schema PINS it to
// `principal` (see event.dwschema), so the pin forces the past Login
// to share the current Read's principal. The correlation is enforced even
// though the policy never wrote it — a directly-written predicate cannot
// bypass a pin.
//
// Positive/negative control across two traces:
//   trace_1: the prior Login is by the SAME principal as the Read → the
//            pinned `callerPrincipal` correlation holds → permitted.
//   trace_2: IDENTICAL except the prior Login is by a DIFFERENT principal →
//            the injected pin forces a mismatch → NOT permitted.
// Without the pin, trace_2 would permit (a Login exists); the pin is what
// excludes the cross-principal match.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
